.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_SET_SSL_VERSION 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_ssl_version ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_get_ssl_method ,
.Nm SSL_set_ssl_method ,
.Nm SSL_get_ssl_method
.Nd choose a new TLS/SSL method
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_ssl_version
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const SSL_METHOD *method"
.Fc
.Ft const SSL_METHOD *
.Fo SSL_CTX_get_ssl_method
.Fa "const SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_set_ssl_method
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "const SSL_METHOD *method"
.Fc
.Ft const SSL_METHOD *
.Fo SSL_get_ssl_method
.Fa "const SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_ssl_version
sets a new default TLS/SSL
.Fa method
for SSL objects newly created from this
.Fa ctx .
Most of the configuration attached to the SSL_CTX object is retained,
with the exception of the configured TLS ciphers, which are reset to the
default values.
SSL objects already created from this SSL_CTX with
.Xr SSL_new 3
are not affected, except when
.Xr SSL_clear 3
is being called, as described below.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_ssl_method
returns the SSL_METHOD which was used to construct the SSL_CTX.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_set_ssl_method
sets a new TLS/SSL
.Fa method
for a particular
.Fa ssl
object.
It may be reset, when
.Xr SSL_clear 3
is called.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_ssl_method
returns a pointer to the TLS/SSL method set in
.Fa ssl .
.Sh NOTES
The available
.Fa method
choices are described in
.Xr SSL_CTX_new 3 .
.Pp
When
.Xr SSL_clear 3
is called and no session is connected to an SSL object, the method of
the SSL object is reset to the method currently set in the corresponding
SSL_CTX object.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_version 3
has unusual semantics and no clear use case; it would usually be
preferable to create a new SSL_CTX object than to try to reuse an
existing one in this fashion.
Its usage is considered deprecated.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_set_ssl_method
cannot be used to change a non-QUIC SSL object to a QUIC SSL object or
vice versa, or change a QUIC SSL object from one QUIC method to another.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The following return values can occur for
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_ssl_version
and
.Fn SSL_set_ssl_method :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The new choice failed, check the error stack to find out the reason.
.It 1
The operation succeeded.
.El
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_ssl_method
and
.Fn SSL_get_ssl_method
always return non-NULL pointers.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr SSL_new 3 ,
.Xr SSL_clear 3 ,
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_set_connect_state 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_ssl_version
was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
